  "Question": "The top of one tree is \\(16\\) feet higher than the top of another tree. The heights of the two trees are in the ratio \\(3:4.\\) In feet, how tall is the taller tree?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\( \\ 48 \\)",
    "B": "\\( \\ 64 \\)",
    "C": "\\( \\ 80 \\)",
    "D": "\\( \\ 96 \\)",
    "E": "\\( \\ 112 \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "The ratio \\(3:4\\) represents three equal height parts for the shorter tree and four of the same parts for the taller tree. Their difference is \\(4-3=1\\) part, so one part is \\(16\\) feet.\n\nThe taller tree has four parts, giving a height of\n\\[\n4\\cdot16=\\boxed{64}\\text{ feet},\n\\]\nchoice B.",
